course: dictionary
lesson: 16146
title: Willpower
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Willpower is the strength of mind to control what you do and stick to what you have decided, even when it is hard. It is a noun, and it names a quality that helps you act the way you want to act.
explain: «It took great willpower for Maya to leave the last biscuit on the plate.» Maya wanted the biscuit, but she chose not to eat it. Her strength of mind made the choice possible, so willpower means strength of mind to control your actions.
explain: You can use willpower to stop a bad habit, or to resist something tempting. «Tom's strong willpower helped him practise the piano every day for a month.» Willpower is useful when you want to do something good for yourself and it is hard to start or keep going.
explain: A good check is to swap in the meaning. Does «Mia used her strength of mind to stop biting her nails» still make sense? Yes, so you have understood willpower correctly.
fact: Willpower is a noun. It means the strength of mind to control your actions and do what you decide.
fact: Willpower is uncountable, so you say «some willpower» or «a lot of willpower», not «a willpower» or «willpowers».
fact: Two common phrases are «strong willpower» and «use willpower».
fact: Willpower helps people stop bad habits or resist temptations, such as a second sweet when they have decided not to have one.
fact: Willpower is about your own choices, so it can help you finish a task even when you would rather do something else.
exercise: «It took great willpower for Maya to leave the last biscuit on the plate.» What does willpower mean here? | *Strength of mind to control what you do | Being good at sport | Being very hungry | Having lots of money
exercise: Which sentence shows a person using willpower? | Tom fell asleep on the sofa before his homework was started. | *Tom switched off the TV and started his homework, even though he wanted to keep watching. | Tom went to the shops to buy some crisps. | Tom lost his pencil case at school.
exercise: Which phrase uses willpower correctly? | willpowered | willpowers | *strong willpower | a willpower
test: «Sam had the willpower to say no to a second slice of cake.» What does willpower tell us about Sam? | Sam had lots of cake | Sam was lost | *Sam had the strength of mind to control what he did | Sam was very tired
test: Mia wants to stop biting her nails. What would help her most? | Buying a new pencil case | Sleeping for longer | *Using her willpower to stop whenever she feels the urge | Eating more sweets
exam: Which sentence uses willpower correctly? | *Ben needs more willpower to finish the race. | Ben has a willpower to finish the race. | Ben willpowered the race. | Ben needs more willpowers to finish the race.
